{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"assiduous-ribbony-mousebird","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nReviewer advisory on Gerrit change 3117 (story e873, which commits .test_durations). To stop gitleaks flagging the profile, `.gitleaks.toml` gained a third targeted allowlist for the fake PEM shape that tests/unit/test_identity_ac1_401a_heldout.py parametrizes on: a BEGIN header, a body of exactly one `x`, an END line, with the newlines literal or escaped. It is scoped by content, not by path.\n\ne873 measured the fix by hand with the review bot's own command (`gitleaks detect --no-banner --no-git --source <dir> --exit-code 0`, no --config): the profile went from 3 findings to 0, and a control file with a real-shaped PEM key (200-character random body) stayed at 1 finding. Nothing in the test suite pins that. The repo already has a harness for exactly this: `test_repo_gitleaks_config_allowlists_doc_throwaway_but_not_real_secret` in tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py. A later edit to the regex could silently broaden the exemption to real keys.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A test reusing that harness asserts that the fake shape (header, one `x`, END line; both literal-newline and escaped-newline forms) yields 0 findings and that a PEM key with a long random body yields 1 (checked: the test, run with gitleaks installed).\n- [ ] The test fails when the allowlist regex is widened to match any PEM body (checked: a recorded mutation run).\n- [ ] `make verify` shows no failure outside the known pandoc set, and the Gerrit change is `Verified +1`.\n","id":"5c17-6b70-c4ae-4f92","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Pin the fake-PEM gitleaks allowlist with a regression test"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793015040962570001,"uuid":"b2725484-9fee-4f79-a8c8-4d5cbb36361b"}